# Line-ending policy.
#
# The Gradle wrapper and shell scripts run in Linux containers (see docker/) and
# on macOS, so they must stay LF even when checked out on Windows. A CRLF in
# gradlew breaks its `#!/bin/sh` shebang and surfaces in the container as:
#   exec ./gradle-tools/gradlew: no such file or directory
gradlew      text eol=lf
*.sh         text eol=lf

# Windows batch files must stay CRLF.
gradlew.bat  text eol=crlf
*.bat        text eol=crlf

# The wrapper jar is binary; never touch its bytes.
*.jar        binary
